From c965895fd38338981496f6441953a98e67db6c63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:14:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(turning): judge a lathe holder body against chuck
 jaws and standing steel

A lathe holder body was judged against the part and stock only; the
fixture laws swept the tool record's 0 x 0 holder cylinder, so an offset
holder striking a chuck jaw passed silently while the op had dropped its
"holder not judged" note.

Every move's meridian pieces now carry the body's clearance spans
against each fixture box: steel turning with the part as its revolved
envelope, standing steel (tailstock, steady rest, table) as a box in the
machine frame, solved exactly per straight tip motion. A strike is a
holder FixtureHit on the move, blocking the post; the post gate's live
fixture walk runs the same law. A tagged fixture with no readable
geometry is named on the op's notes.

Fixes #1037

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
